inear local reads under uniform descendant blindness, not the complete available effect algebra, and explicitly retains availability premises (D28 §23). On 0→p→l with F=I and equal-total preparations g e_0 and g e_l, the initial own-grade equality is 0 vs 0, and post-pruning contrast is 0 vs g. However, the initial incoming field-edge contrast is 0 vs a_1 g, meaning a receiver with complete local-field access is already informed. This confirms that restricted own-grade access is a supplied interface, and formal selected-read blindness does not entail complete receiver blindness.\"\n  ],\n  \"native_bridge_status\": \"NOT_DERIVED\",\n  \"next_native_obligation\": \"Start with an existing native receiver-owned record and its actual state-to-record association. Establish the record's event ledger, complete receiver blindness before the event, two positive local responses (with at least one nonzero), and one already justified post-event effect with nonzero contrast and retained source/reference association.\"\n}",
